## 25. Why the Hour Hand Matters

A common mistake is to assume **3:30** means the hour hand sits exactly on the 3. It does not — the hour hand keeps moving between hour marks as the minutes pass:

$\theta_h = 30(3) + 0.5(30) = 105°$, while the minute hand is at $\theta_m = 6(30) = 180°$. The angle between them is $180 - 105 = 75°$, not the $90°$ you'd get by wrongly assuming the hour hand stays put on the 3.

